WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.326 --> 00:00:02.287
Have you...

00:00:05.415 --> 00:00:06.750
ever been in love?

00:00:08.251 --> 00:00:10.128
Yep. Nancy Wheeler.

00:00:10.211 --> 00:00:11.588
First semester, senior year.

00:00:11.671 --> 00:00:13.131
[imitates gunshot, chuckles]

00:00:13.381 --> 00:00:14.799
Oh, my God.

00:00:15.592 --> 00:00:17.260
She's such a priss.

00:00:17.802 --> 00:00:18.720
[Steve] Hm.

00:00:19.846 --> 00:00:21.139
Turns out, not really.

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:24.434
[scoffs]
Are you still in love with Nancy?

00:00:26.644 --> 00:00:28.021
-No.
-Why not?

00:00:30.815 --> 00:00:33.485
I think it's because I found someone
who's a little bit better for me.

00:00:34.277 --> 00:00:35.570
[chuckles] It's crazy.

00:00:36.488 --> 00:00:38.323
Ever since Dustin got home,
he's been saying,

00:00:38.406 --> 00:00:41.201
"You know, you gotta find your Suzie.
You gotta find your Suzie."

00:00:41.284 --> 00:00:42.619
Wait, who's Suzie?

00:00:42.702 --> 00:00:45.455
It's some girl from camp,
I guess his girlfriend.

00:00:45.538 --> 00:00:48.875
To be honest with you,
I'm not 100% sure she's even real.

00:00:50.585 --> 00:00:52.712
But that's not--
that's not really the point.

00:00:52.796 --> 00:00:55.757
That doesn't matter. The point is,
this girl, you know, the one that I like,

00:00:57.383 --> 00:01:01.054
it's somebody that I...
didn't even talk to in school.

00:01:02.597 --> 00:01:04.140
And I don't even know why.

00:01:04.224 --> 00:01:07.101
Maybe 'cause Tommy H.
would've made fun of me or...

00:01:08.353 --> 00:01:09.479
I wouldn't be...

00:01:10.688 --> 00:01:11.689
prom king.

00:01:13.525 --> 00:01:17.028
It's stupid. I mean, Dustin's right,
it's all just a bunch of bullshit anyways.

00:01:17.111 --> 00:01:18.404
Because, when I think about it,

00:01:18.488 --> 00:01:20.782
I should've been hanging out
with this girl the whole time.

00:01:20.865 --> 00:01:23.201
First of all, she's hilarious.
She's so funny.

00:01:23.284 --> 00:01:26.162
I feel like, this summer,
I have laughed harder

00:01:26.246 --> 00:01:27.497
than I have laughed...

00:01:28.206 --> 00:01:29.666
in a really long time.

00:01:29.749 --> 00:01:31.084
And she's smart.

00:01:32.502 --> 00:01:33.878
Way smarter than me.

00:01:35.296 --> 00:01:38.424
You know, she can crack, like,
top secret Russian codes and...

00:01:40.009 --> 00:01:43.137
You know? She's honestly unlike anyone
I've ever even met before.

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:49.394
Robin?

00:01:50.228 --> 00:01:51.396
[tapping on stall]

00:01:54.649 --> 00:01:56.276
Robin, did you just OD in there?

00:01:57.151 --> 00:01:58.528
No. [sighs]

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:00.196
I...

00:02:00.905 --> 00:02:02.448
am still alive.

00:02:04.701 --> 00:02:05.827
[deep sigh]

00:02:12.834 --> 00:02:14.127
[Robin] The floor's disgusting.

00:02:14.711 --> 00:02:18.298
Yeah, well, I already got a bunch of blood
and puke on my shirt, so...

00:02:20.758 --> 00:02:21.843
What do you think?

00:02:22.886 --> 00:02:23.803
About?

00:02:24.304 --> 00:02:25.555
This girl.

00:02:25.972 --> 00:02:26.931
She sounds awesome.

00:02:27.015 --> 00:02:29.726
She is awesome. And what about the guy?

00:02:29.809 --> 00:02:32.979
I think he's on drugs,
and he's not thinking straight.

00:02:33.062 --> 00:02:35.773
Really? 'Cause I think he's thinking
a lot more clearly than usual.

00:02:36.232 --> 00:02:37.233
He's not.

00:02:39.319 --> 00:02:40.278
Look...

00:02:41.487 --> 00:02:44.115
he doesn't even know this girl.

00:02:44.616 --> 00:02:46.284
And if he did know her,

00:02:46.492 --> 00:02:48.119
like-- like really know her,

00:02:48.912 --> 00:02:51.664
I don't think he'd even want to be
her friend.

00:02:51.748 --> 00:02:54.167
No, that's not true. No way is that true.

00:02:54.250 --> 00:02:55.835
Listen to me, Steve.

00:02:56.294 --> 00:02:58.379
It's shocked me to my core,

00:02:58.922 --> 00:03:00.381
but I like you.

00:03:01.174 --> 00:03:02.675
I really like you.

00:03:03.468 --> 00:03:05.219
But I'm not like your other friends.

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:08.681
And I'm not like Nancy Wheeler.

00:03:08.765 --> 00:03:10.850
Robin, that's exactly why I like you.

00:03:10.934 --> 00:03:11.809
[Robin scoffs]

00:03:11.893 --> 00:03:14.437
Do you remember what I said
about Click's class?

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:17.982
About me being jealous and, like,
obsessed?

00:03:18.816 --> 00:03:19.651
Yeah.

00:03:19.734 --> 00:03:22.987
It isn't because I had a crush on you.

00:03:25.114 --> 00:03:26.199
It's because...

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:29.869
she wouldn't stop staring at you.

00:03:31.704 --> 00:03:32.705
Mrs. Click?

00:03:32.789 --> 00:03:33.831
[chuckles]

00:03:35.917 --> 00:03:37.418
Tammy Thompson.

00:03:39.128 --> 00:03:40.713
I wanted her to look at me.

00:03:41.714 --> 00:03:45.009
But... she couldn't
pull her eyes away from you

00:03:45.093 --> 00:03:48.179
and your stupid hair.

00:03:49.222 --> 00:03:51.766
And I didn't understand,
because you would get

00:03:52.642 --> 00:03:55.478
bagel crumbs all over the floor.

00:03:56.479 --> 00:03:58.898
And you asked dumb questions.

00:03:58.982 --> 00:04:01.192
And you were a douchebag.

00:04:01.693 --> 00:04:03.653
And-- And you didn't even like her and...

00:04:03.736 --> 00:04:05.113
I would go home...

00:04:05.905 --> 00:04:08.241
and just scream into my pillow.

00:04:09.075 --> 00:04:11.327
But Tammy Thompson's a girl.

00:04:13.037 --> 00:04:13.997
[softly] Steve.

00:04:14.664 --> 00:04:15.498
Yeah?

00:04:19.794 --> 00:04:20.628
Oh.

00:04:21.462 --> 00:04:22.296
Oh.

00:04:24.298 --> 00:04:25.341
Holy shit.

00:04:26.217 --> 00:04:27.051
Yeah.

00:04:28.136 --> 00:04:28.970
Holy shit.

00:04:40.940 --> 00:04:42.025
Steve...

00:04:42.984 --> 00:04:44.193
did you OD over there?

00:04:45.028 --> 00:04:46.320
No, I just, uh...

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:48.781
just thinking.

00:04:48.865 --> 00:04:49.866
Okay.

00:04:52.118 --> 00:04:53.202
I mean, yeah.

00:04:54.954 --> 00:04:57.582
Tammy Thompson, you know,
she's cute and all, but...

00:04:59.083 --> 00:05:00.043
I mean,

00:05:00.126 --> 00:05:01.461
she's a total dud.

00:05:01.544 --> 00:05:02.754
She is not.

00:05:03.171 --> 00:05:05.548
Yes, she is.
She wants to be, like, a singer.

00:05:05.631 --> 00:05:07.633
She wants to move to, like,
Nashville and shit.

00:05:07.717 --> 00:05:10.136
-She has dreams.
-She can't even hold a tune.

00:05:10.219 --> 00:05:12.555
She's practically tone-deaf.
Have you heard her?

00:05:12.638 --> 00:05:13.848
-[Robin chuckles]
-All the time.

00:05:13.931 --> 00:05:16.267
[singing atonally]
♪ You see me now tonight ♪

00:05:16.350 --> 00:05:17.810
-Shut up.
-♪ You see me... ♪

00:05:17.894 --> 00:05:20.021
-She does not sound like that.
-She sounds exactly--

00:05:20.104 --> 00:05:21.981
-That's a great impersonation of her.
-She does not.

00:05:22.065 --> 00:05:23.149
You sound like a Muppet.

00:05:23.232 --> 00:05:24.734
She sounds like a Muppet.

00:05:24.817 --> 00:05:26.861
She sounds like a Muppet giving birth.

00:05:26.944 --> 00:05:27.945
[both laughing]

00:05:28.029 --> 00:05:30.573
[sings like Kermit]
♪ And if you could hold me tight ♪

00:05:30.656 --> 00:05:33.242
[both sing atonally]
♪ We'll be holding on forever ♪

00:05:33.326 --> 00:05:35.119
-Exactly.
-[laughs] I know!

00:05:40.958 --> 00:05:41.834
Okay.

00:05:41.918 --> 00:05:42.752
What the hell?

00:05:43.669 --> 00:05:46.047
[both laugh]

